  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem, where Power Display switches to a different profile after the PC wakes from sleep. The closest tickets describe different problems. PowerToys#48774 is about a profile linked to Light Switch not triggering on wake. PowerToys#47776 is about monitor-specific settings being forgotten after a monitor power cycle. PowerToys#48428 is about a monitor not turning back on after standby. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. Attach a PowerToys bug report ZIP, which you can generate from Settings > General > Report a bug. Also include whether Light Switch profile linking or any power-state options are enabled, and whether the issue happens without the docking station. As a workaround, you can re-select the dimmed profile after wake.\"}",
